# Left unset on purpose in development: the app then calls a relative /api,
# which the dev server proxies to the backend over the same origin the page
# came from. That keeps one certificate exception covering the page, the API
# and the meeting socket instead of three.
#
# Set it only when the API is somewhere the proxy cannot reach, and remember
# that a browser shows no certificate warning for a WebSocket — it just fails
# — so that origin has to be one the browser already trusts.
# VITE_API_URL=https://localhost:4000/api
